// Test: bugfixes/codegen_number_tostring_in_i32_context
// Semantic: codegen must dispatch Number.toString to float_to_string, not int_to_string
// Tracking: 322f839eb828
// Fixed in: compiler 0.33.77
//
// Regression pin for dashboard fingerprint 322f839eb828
// (codegen-f64-in-i32-slot).
//
// Pre-fix: `string s = toString(number_expr)` compiled with an incorrect
// MIR dispatch that pushed the f64 value directly into a bridge slot
// expecting i32, producing WASM with "type mismatch: expected i32,
// found f64" at codegen time. The clean-errors project surfaced this
// on the tarball-upload endpoint (dashboard fp 322f839eb828, reported
// against cln 0.33.66); dev-queue entry f26672a3b9a11308 captured the
// same shape with this 4-line repro. Byte-pattern signature of the
// broken instruction stream:
//     21 00 20 00 21 01 20 01 10 64 21 02 20 02 21 03
//
// Fix: src/mir/mir_builder.rs early-dispatches Number.toString to
// float_to_string (commit 727db5c3, shipped v0.33.77). The generated
// WASM now inserts the float→string bridge on the number path
// instead of routing through the integer-typed default.
//
// Success criteria: this pin compiles cleanly AND the emitted WASM
// validates. Runtime execution prints the string representation of
// 3.14; formatting is float_to_string's responsibility, not this
// pin's — any string-like output containing "3.14" is a valid pass.
//
// Fixed in: compiler 0.33.77
// Expected output:
//   3.14

start:
	number x = 3.14
	string s = toString(x)
	print(s)
